From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:41:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scripts: sign-file: finalize the signer with BoringSSL

The LineageOS kernel host tools link sign-file against BoringSSL. Its
CMS_add1_signer() rejects CMS_PARTIAL, which requests configuring the
signer in multiple steps. sign-file does not perform that configuration;
it supplies the certificate, key and digest together.

Keep CMS_PARTIAL when creating the SignedData, but clear it when adding
the complete signer. This retains the detached, attribute-free module
signature format and allows CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_ALL to work without
replacing the Android host toolchain or disabling module verification.

Source: local integration fix for LineageOS 24 kernel host tools.
Base: msm8953-mainline/linux 755ffc44d5d8442adeec8bbaa02108478089c4d7.
---
 scripts/sign-file.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/sign-file.c b/scripts/sign-file.c
--- a/scripts/sign-file.c
+++ b/scripts/sign-file.c
@@ -287,7 +287,8 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 		cms = CMS_sign(NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, flags);
 		ERR(!cms, "CMS_sign");
 
-		ERR(!CMS_add1_signer(cms, x509, private_key, digest_algo, flags),
+		ERR(!CMS_add1_signer(cms, x509, private_key, digest_algo,
+				     flags & ~CMS_PARTIAL),
 		    "CMS_add1_signer");
 		ERR(CMS_final(cms, bm, NULL, flags) != 1,
 		    "CMS_final");
